Give LFG-raid-fill bots a valid LFG role so proposal packets don't carry
role=0 (PLAYER_ROLE_NONE).
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp, RandomPlayerbotMgr::FillLfgRaidGroup()

Why: FillLfgRaidGroup() inserts idle bots straight into a group via
group->AddMember(bot), bypassing the normal LFG queue/role-check flow
entirely, so the bot's LFG role never gets set (stays PLAYER_ROLE_NONE).
SendLfgProposalUpdate (LFGHandler.cpp) writes that role straight onto the
wire with no validation. The 3.3.5 client's FrameXML then throws
"Interface\FrameXML\LFGFrame.lua:337: Unknown role: UNKNOWN" trying to
pick a role icon for it when the player accepts the dungeon-ready pop-up.

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ RandomPlayerbotMgr::FillLfgRaidGroup(Group* group, uint32 maxPlayers, uint8 minLevel, uint8 maxLevel)
         if (!group->AddMember(bot))
             break;
+        // Bots added this way skip the normal LFG queue/role-check flow
+        // entirely, so their LFG role stays PLAYER_ROLE_NONE. The dungeon
+        // proposal packet writes that role straight to the wire with no
+        // validation (LFGHandler.cpp SendLfgProposalUpdate), and the client's
+        // FrameXML errors "Unknown role: UNKNOWN" trying to render an icon
+        // for it. A flat DAMAGE role here is just for that packet/icon --
+        // it doesn't affect the bot's actual combat AI role.
+        sLFGMgr->SetRoles(bot->GetGUID(), lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_DAMAGE);
         ++added;
